# Q: does a checkpoint restore the world it was taken from — verified, and honestly priced?
#
#   MiVic.Game.exe --probe tools/probe/checkpoints.probe --probe-out artifacts/probe/checkpoints.txt
#
# The standard skirmish, nothing placed and nothing cleared: a world whose external inputs are
# all in its command log, which is the precondition a restore stands on. Orders go through the
# player's path so the log carries them, the match runs on, and then the same position is
# rebuilt two ways and asked to be the same world.
#
# What each command answers:
#
#   - `save` takes a named checkpoint and reports its size, because a checkpoint that had
#     quietly become a state dump would show itself in that number;
#   - `rewind` restores from the nearest keyframe with the live command log carried forward,
#     verified the complete way — the same position rebuilt from tick zero must carry the same
#     hash — and reports the cost in ticks replayed and in milliseconds, which is the trade
#     the keyframes exist to win;
#   - `restore` puts the saved world back where it was, its hash compared against the hash
#     the save recorded;
#   - `checkpoints` is the inventory: what has been saved and which ticks the keyframes stand
#     on.
#
# A world whose history is not all in its command log — a fixture that spawned or cleared
# entities directly, for one — fails the hash check here, by design: a checkpoint that restores
# a different world silently would be worse than no checkpoint at all.

# --- run the opening, and put a few orders in the log -------------------------------------------
tick 30
order 259 move -40 120
order 260 move 60 140
tick 40

# --- a checkpoint worth coming back to -----------------------------------------------------------
save base

# --- run on, so the keyframes accumulate and the log grows past the save ------------------------
tick 130

# --- the rewind: back to the saved tick, from the keyframe beneath it ---------------------------
rewind 70

# --- and the save, independently: the same tick, from its own handle ----------------------------
restore base

# --- what the store ended up holding --------------------------------------------------------------
checkpoints
